<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
  <title>Your .com is taken. Here’s what {{total}} SF startups did. | Domain Hound</title>
  <meta name="description" content="The top 3 endings among {{total}} Bay Area YC startups: {{description}}.">
  <meta property="og:type" content="article">
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="Domain Hound">
  <meta property="og:title" content="Your .com is taken. Here’s what {{total}} SF startups did.">
  <meta property="og:description" content="The top 3 endings among {{total}} Bay Area YC startups: {{description}}.">
  <meta property="og:image" content="https://domainhound.dev/sf/share.png">
  <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
  <meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
  <meta property="og:image:alt" content="The top 3 endings among {{total}} Bay Area YC startups: {{description}}.">
  <meta property="og:url" content="https://domainhound.dev/sf/">
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://domainhound.dev/sf/">
  <link rel="icon" href="/assets/hound-mark.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/home.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/sf/palette.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/sf/page.css">
  <script type="module" src="/sf/page.mjs"></script>

</head>
<body>
<header><div class="frame mast">
  <a class="paper-art" href="/" aria-label="Domain Hound home">
    <span class="paper-word first">Domain</span><span class="paper-word second">Hound</span>
    <span class="paper-dog"><img src="/assets/hound-mark.svg" width="180" height="180" alt=""></span>
  </a>
  <a class="jump" href="#check">Check a name</a>
</div></header>
<main>
  <section class="intro"><div class="frame spread">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Bay Area YC directory</p>
      <h1><span>Your .com is taken.</span> <span>Here’s what {{total}} SF startups did.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">You don’t always need the .com.</p>
    </div>
    <section class="ticket" aria-labelledby="leaders-title">
      <div class="ticket-top"><h2 id="leaders-title">The top 3</h2><span>Sites · Share</span></div>
      <ol id="leaders">{{leaders}}</ol>
      <svg class="postcard-scene" viewBox="0 0 400 110" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <defs>
          <g id="gate-span" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <!-- The nearer tower and deck sit higher in the perspective view. -->
            <path d="M-4 77Q37 69 97 12Q167 112 279 44Q326 87 404 87" stroke-width="2.6"/>
            <path d="M18 71v14m19-24v24m19-37v37m20-54v54m42-48v49m18-32v33m19-23v24m19-19v19m19-16v17m19-18v18m20-22v23m19-30v30m17-40v41m30-28v29m18-18v19m19-12v13m20-9v9m21-5v6" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <path d="M-4 84l408 10" stroke-width="5"/>
            <path d="M90 101l3-94h3l-1 94zm12 0l-2-94h3l4 94zm171 0l3-63h2l-1 63zm9 0l-2-63h2l4 63z" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/>
            <path d="M94 14h7m-7 7h7m-8 16h9m-10 16h11m-11 17h12m172-26h6m-7 9h8m-8 12h8m-9 13h10" stroke-width="3"/>
          </g>
        </defs>
        <path fill="var(--mist)" d="M0 0h400v110H0z"/>
        <circle cx="331" cy="30" r="18" fill="var(--leaf)"/>
        <path fill="var(--mint)" d="M0 60q30-14 59-9t52 5q25-1 53-12t55-6q30 6 55 24t57 9q40-13 69-8v47H0z"/>
        <path fill="var(--paper)" d="M0 67h70q8 0 8 3t-8 3H0zm180-7h74q7 0 7 2.5t-7 2.5h-74q-6 0-6-2.5t6-2.5z"/>
        <use href="#gate-span"/>
        <path fill="currentColor" d="M0 76q16 0 34 9l32 17q8 4 17 8H0zm400 7q-23 0-44 10t-50 17h94z"/>
      </svg>
    </section>
  </div></section>
  <div class="ranking-band"><div class="frame ranking-spread">
    <section><h2>The top 10 endings</h2><ol id="ranking">{{ranking}}</ol></section>
    <section class="reason"><h2>Why not .com?</h2>
      <strong>{{takenPct}}%</strong>
      <p>Among startups on other endings, {{registered}} of {{nonCom}} matching .coms were taken when checked.</p>
      <p>Buying one from its owner can cost a lot.</p>
    </section>
  </div></div>
  <section class="examples-band"><div class="frame">
    <h2>It works on other endings too</h2>
    <div class="examples">{{groups}}</div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="chart-band"><div class="frame">
    <h2>.ai over time</h2>
    <p class="deck">{{firstAi}}% in {{first}}, {{lastAi}}% in {{latest}}.</p>
    <div class="legend"><span><i class="com"></i>.com</span><span><i class="ai"></i>.ai</span><span><i class="rest"></i>Other endings</span></div>
    <div class="plot">
      <div class="axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>100%</span><span>50%</span><span>0%</span></div>
      <div class="years">{{bars}}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="batch-readout"><select aria-label="YC batch" id="batch-select" disabled>{{options}}</select><span id="batch-summary" role="status">{{summary}}</span></div>
    <details class="batch-details"><summary>All endings in this batch</summary>
      <table><caption>{{latest}}</caption><thead><tr><th>Ending</th><th>Sites</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{tableRows}}</tbody></table>
    </details>
  </div></section>
  <section class="facts-band"><div class="frame">
    <h2>Behind the dot</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <article><h3>Compound names</h3><strong>{{compound}}</strong><p>names resemble joined dictionary words.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Branded prefixes</h3><strong>{{get}} / {{try}}</strong><p>used “get” / “try” before the exact brand.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Shortest to longest</h3><strong>{{shortest}} to {{longest}}</strong><p>characters, from <b>{{shortestDomain}}</b> to <b>{{longestDomain}}</b>.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="choice-band"><div class="frame choice">
    <h2>How to choose</h2>
    <ol><li>Take the exact .com if it’s available at the usual registration price.</li>
      <li>Try .ai, .dev or .io if it fits your work.</li>
      <li>Favor your exact brand over a longer .com.</li>
      <li>Check app stores and trademarks.</li></ol>
  </div></section>
  <section id="check" class="check-band"><div class="frame">
    <h2>Check a name</h2>
    <form id="check-form" hidden autocomplete="off"><label for="candidate">Name or domain</label><div class="field">
      <input id="candidate" type="text" maxlength="253" required placeholder="Your startup name" autocapitalize="none" spellcheck="false">
      <button type="submit">Check endings</button>
    </div></form>
    <noscript><p>Turn on JavaScript for a live domain check.</p></noscript>
    <p id="check-status" role="status"></p><ul id="matches"></ul>
  </div></section>
  <section class="method"><div class="frame">
    <h2>Method and sources</h2>
    <p>One site per Bay Area startup, {{first}} to {{latest}}. {{excluded}} lacked websites.</p>
    <p><a href="https://rdap.verisign.com/com/v1/help">Verisign RDAP</a>, {{checked}}. We matched lowercase brand letters and digits. {{redirected}} .coms redirected to listed sites. Launch-day availability and ownership are unknown.</p>
    <p><a href="{{source}}">Directory snapshot</a> · <a href="https://publicsuffix.org/list/">Public Suffix List</a> · <a href="https://www.nltk.org/howto/wordnet.html">WordNet</a></p>
    <div class="foot-links"><button id="share" hidden>Share this page</button><span id="share-status" role="status"></span></div>
  </div></section>
</main>
<footer><div class="frame"><p>Not affiliated with Y Combinator. <a href="https://www.ycombinator.com/companies">Data from YC's public directory.</a></p><a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a></div></footer>
<script type="application/json" id="batch-data">{{batchData}}</script>
</body>
</html>
